#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0c7c6d9-551c-5844-83f9-f3e199afc52f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341671} {:answer/id #uuid "7aba49aa-8dab-5788-b79e-9e9783b4b204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341672} {:answer/id #uuid "4f46b4eb-16b2-5b9e-a3de-404f078480e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341673} {:answer/id #uuid "271a81cd-eaa3-5ec9-93e1-61a648e3a523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341674} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ad553c-d7b9-5104-9e02-fc5b565fbd8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271a81cd-eaa3-5ec9-93e1-61a648e3a523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341674} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6d66fdf-bbb7-5d6e-b93c-ae1dcaac0321" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "302cb8da-ded5-5011-8c1e-b60b334aa94d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20976" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ defined on the closed interval $-2\\le x\\le 2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $45$\n- The global minimum value is $-14$\n- The global maximum value is $18$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)-(x+2) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-2,\\,-1,\\,1,$ and the endpoints $x=-2,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =3(-2)^{4}+8(-2)^{3}-6(-2)^{2}-24(-2)+5=13 \\\\ f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}+8(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-24(-1)+5=18 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}+8(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-24(1)+5=-14 \\\\ f(2) & =3(2)^{4}+8(2)^{3}-6(2)^{2}-24(2)+5=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(2)=45,$ so the global maximum is $45.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(1)=-14,$ so the global minimum is $-14.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/9b48417439d0e018250328b92561732dd9f4c8bbec157daf33287b20dac7c41f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "972c7300-e47b-5609-b05d-a84f033a1710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341678} {:answer/id #uuid "45d49fd1-9515-5441-9384-826e833953fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341679} {:answer/id #uuid "5046e823-0a23-5868-8664-1aa8b8386754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341680} {:answer/id #uuid "c1652d0e-a320-5685-bbe4-ca522361f00a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341681} {:answer/id #uuid "10d5d0e1-a548-590f-a8b1-8ae247f03c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5046e823-0a23-5868-8664-1aa8b8386754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341680} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b429e3f-ab7f-58c0-8488-208ee655eff3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6187976-1be0-519f-b378-82888b36e23d" :question/math-academy-id "q-2689" :question/problem "Find the global minimum value of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-16x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-2)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-3,1]$, the critical points are $x=-2,0,$ and the endpoints $x=-3,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{4}-8(-3)^{2}=9 \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2)^{4}-8(-2)^{2}=-16 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{4}-8(0)^{2}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{4}-8(1)^{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-3)=9,$ so the global maximum is $9.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-2)=-16,$ so the global minimum is $-16.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/e57ff9bc04fb9d9db592dda6aac9c364fd5f2e6fcd52968627b1e0271919f5bb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d874ba62-7ea7-5fe3-9ad7-237c77d3d2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341685} {:answer/id #uuid "f32d00c1-e054-583d-95bc-7220e2293115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341686} {:answer/id #uuid "c53dc68a-ad5b-53c4-b840-eeb818a40bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341687} {:answer/id #uuid "9459ae53-92cb-536c-88e7-3104b0184d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341688} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdfb5d2-6557-59f7-bcd3-5f9c49cf1d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f32d00c1-e054-583d-95bc-7220e2293115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341686} :answer-field/id #uuid "6461a09e-135d-5733-8160-60ec782fc040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc729d7c-7a1c-595c-bd37-276a0411df84" :question/math-academy-id "q-2698" :question/problem "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-9x+3$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le -1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-9x+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3{x}^{2}-12x-9,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-12x-9 & =0 \\\\ -3({x}^{2}+4x+3) & =0 \\\\ -3(x+3)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-3,-1,$ which coincide with the endpoints of the given interval.\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =-(-3)^{3}-6(-3)^{2}-9(-3)+3=3 \\\\ f(-1) & =-(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-9(-1)+3=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-1)=7,$ so the global maximum is $7.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(-3)=3,$ so the global minimum is $3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/2eca6b83a3f99ca87a70e381490e99c98e80a535cd3051a4cdd0740f82de577b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa8182fb-7429-5094-99af-5c3a2db42d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8182fb-7429-5094-99af-5c3a2db42d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341692} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecafe37-e989-54bd-abcf-774b5973feda" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55363c3c-02e7-50b7-9197-4efdcda472d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-344460" :question/problem "The global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)-x(2x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 1-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-1$ does not belong to the interval $[0,2],$ the critical points are $x=1$ and the endpoints $x=0,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}+1}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ f(2) & =\\frac{2}{{2}^{2}+1}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The least value is $f(0)=0,$ so the global minimum is $0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/463d11ca52d41491a6184a1d7d39692af43e53aa0fd470324a8f8e999c842811.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71e24774-12a1-53e2-bc02-7f3feafd73b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341695} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d21d9e-6411-5640-8b0a-bc10e5b573ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341696} {:answer/id #uuid "aee9966f-818a-59bc-8bd9-4e0a475857f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341697} {:answer/id #uuid "4f08028a-09db-5b71-a04e-5630aad6071c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341698} {:answer/id #uuid "12bbd708-8947-507a-a8e4-aba51f9837ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71e24774-12a1-53e2-bc02-7f3feafd73b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341695} :answer-field/id #uuid "c84366d3-19cf-5173-8fa9-d3384145cc07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "234b945a-d7d5-5235-a923-8856a2131a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-79341" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $\\frac{9}{e}$\n- The global maximum value is $4$\n- The global minimum value is $e$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2(x-2){e}^{x}+(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x-2){e}^{x}[2+x-2] \\\\  & =x(x-2){e}^{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nx(x-2){e}^{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\\,2.\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1-2)^{2}{e}^{-1}=\\frac{9}{e}≈3.31 \\\\ f(0) & =(0-2)^{2}{e}^{0}=4 \\\\ f(1) & =(1-2)^{2}{e}^{1}=e≈2.72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=4,$ so the global maximum is $4.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=e,$ so the global minimum is $e.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/adeb7eb92f270a216f30cd0466e91d0363c5a50b17053316e6e9f44d0dfaaf23.png)"}]}
